hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27694","Haddathana Affan: Haddathana Hammam, he said: Haddathana Muhammad ibn Juhadah, he said: al-Mughirah ibn Abd Allah al-Yashkuri narrated to me from his father, he said: I went to Kufa to bring mules. He said: So I came to the market and it had not yet been set up. He said: I said to a companion of mine: If we entered the mosque, whose place was then among the date sellers, and in it was a man of Qays called Ibn al-Muntafiq, while he was saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was described to me and adorned, so I sought him at Mina, and it was said to me: He is at Arafat. So I reached him and crowded upon him, and it was said to me: Keep away from the path of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So he said: Leave the man; he has a need, what is it? He said: So I crowded upon him until I reached him. He said: So I took hold of the halter of the mount of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, or he said: its reins, thus Muhammad narrated, until the necks of our two mounts differed. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not repel me, or he said: he did not rebuke me, thus Muhammad narrated. He said: I said: Two things I ask you about: what saves me from the Fire and what enters me into Paradise. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, looked to the sky, then lowered his head, then turned to me with his face. He said: If you were brief in the question, you have magnified and lengthened, so comprehend from me then: Worship Allah, associate nothing with Him, establish the prescribed prayer, give the obligatory zakat, fast Ramadan, and what you love that people do to you, do it to them, and what you hate that people bring to you, leave the people from it. Then he said: Free the way of the mount."
"27695","Haddathana Waki', from Amr ibn Hassan, meaning al-Masli, he said: al-Mughirah ibn Abd Allah al-Yashkuri narrated to me from his father, he said: I entered the mosque of Kufa when its mosque was first built, while it was among the date sellers in those days and its walls were of sahla, and there was a man narrating to the people. He said: The Farewell pilgrimage of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, reached me. He said: So I followed a she-camel of my camels, then I went out until I sat for him on the road of Arafah, or I stood for him on the road of Arafah. He said: And there were riders, and I recognized the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, among them by the description. So a man before him said: Clear the road of the riders. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Woe to him, leave him, for he has a need. So I drew near to him until the heads of the two she-camels differed. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, guide me to a deed that enters me into Paradise and saves me from the Fire. He said: Bravo, bravo; if you were brief in the address, you have conveyed in the question. Fear Allah, associate nothing with Allah, establish prayer, give zakat, perform hajj to the House, and fast Ramadan. Clear the road of the riders."
